camera.device@1.0-impl: cookie fallback, ANativeWindowBuffer preview, and
sensor orientation override

Three fixes to the AOSP HAL1 wrapper, all needed by MediaTek's legacy blobs:

1) libcam.client.so calls the get_memory callback without forwarding the
   cookie passed to set_callbacks(), so `user` arrives NULL and
   object->mDeviceCallback faults at offset 0x8c. Only one CameraDevice is
   ever open in the process, so record it at open() and fall back to it.

2) sDequeueBuffer handed back the address of a standalone buffer_handle_t.
   A real ANativeWindow returns a pointer *into* an ANativeWindowBuffer, and
   MediaTek's blob recovers that object by offsetting back from it. Wrap each
   imported handle in a GraphicBuffer and return &gb->handle.

3) The HAL reports a phone-style SENSOR_ORIENTATION (270) although the sensor
   is landscape-mounted and the driver flips it 180 degrees, so frames arrive
   upright and any client that rotates by SENSOR_ORIENTATION comes out
   sideways. The value originates in libcam.utils.so
   (DevMetaInfo::queryDeviceWantedOrientation) and cannot be fixed in the
   blobs, so honour ro.camera.sensor_orientation here, where both HAL1 clients
   and the camera2 legacy shim pick it up. See patches/0009-* for the property.

